    "encrypted": "false",
    "long_instructions": "## From JSON to UI\r\n\r\nBefore you build your app, you need to decide how the data will look to your users. \r\n\r\n**Your Task:**\r\n*   **Review the JSON:** Read over the sample artist JSON data below.\r\n*   **Choose a Layout:** Decide if you are building a **Playlist** (vertical list) or an **Album Gallery** (grid of cards).\r\n*   **Sketch a Wireframe:** Draw a mockup for **one list row** or **one album card**. Use labels and arrows to show where specific JSON fields will go. \r\n\r\n_Note: You don't have to display all of the data._\r\n\r\n::: details [**Artist JSON data**]\r\n```\r\n{\r\n  \"track\": \"Electric Sparks\",  \r\n  \"artist\": \"Neon Echoes\",\r\n  \"popularity\": 63,\r\n  \"genres\": [\"Indie rock\", \"Dream pop\"],\r\n  \"id\": \"7FAKEechoes001\",\r\n  \"images\": [\r\n    {\r\n      \"url\": \"https://i.scdn.co/image/ab67616d00001e02echoes001\",\r\n      \"height\": 300,\r\n      \"width\": 300\r\n    }\r\n  ],\r\n  \"followers\": {\r\n    \"total\": 184230\r\n  }\r\n}\r\n\r\n```\r\n:::",
